oximately 2:09–41:54. Substantive moderator interventions and their dependent replies are excluded, removing approximately 20:31 (51.6%) of that window and leaving approximately 19:14 of eligible conversation. The exclusions include host-led exchanges about book tone, selective evidence, divine intervention, religious upbringing, antisemitism, and moral necessity. Introductions and all audience Q&A are also unscored. Neither speaker receives credit or penalty for excluded material; the scores do not assess the complete event."},{"id":"craig-pigliucci-christian-god-2001","number":"271","notice":"This assessment covers both opening statements, both rounds of rebuttal, and both closing statements (approximately 6:31–1:39:05). The moderator’s subsequent third-position interlude and the entire audience Q&A, including both speakers’ answers, are excluded. Neither side receives credit or penalty for excluded material; these scores assess the approved formal debate, not the complete event."},{"id":"craig-dacey-god-existence-2004","number":"273","notice":"This assessment covers both opening statements, both rounds of rebuttal, and both closing statements (approximately 5:00–1:40:07). The entire audience Q&A, including both speakers’ answers and dependent replies, is excluded. Neither side receives credit or penalty for excluded material; these scores assess the approved formal debate, not the complete event."},{"id":"shermer-scrivener-good-without-god-2024","number":"277","notice":"By explicit editorial approval, this assessment scores only Michael Shermer and Glen Scrivener across the complete substantive exchange. Moderator Vince Vitale supplies substantive philosophical questions and challenges beyond the ordinary incidental-host allowance; his contributions remain context, and the debaters’ own replies remain eligible for assessment. No argument or score is assigned to a debater merely because Vitale advances it. Unequal questioning is considered when selecting moves and